 `tool_versions.json` records the named iterations, component hashes, scope and aggregate tool digest. These count documented method generations, not every individual edit or commit. Unknown historical patch rounds are not invented. Existing release names such as `sf7-rc1` and `ru1_v3_edits` remain intact alongside the new tool versions. Run `python scripts/harvest/build_filter_versions.py` only when intentionally issuing a new exact build; it fingerprints the working files and existing artifacts.
@@ -28,11 +29,19 @@ The owner accepted the current segmentation policy as-is on 18 October 2026. Its
 4. Schedule every relevant corrective, including polytonic expectations even when marks are absent, Cyrillic spans with orthography eligibility, numeric spans and dash tags. An absent sparse-overlay record is not a no-change verdict.
 5. Validate every result against parent, split, crop, raw-text hash, tool version and implementation digest. Combine compatible raw-parent spans, coalesce identical edits and hold conflicting overlaps. UTF-8 byte patches are converted only at verified character boundaries.
 6. Re-inventory the merged label and schedule newly relevant routes until stable. Recheck candidate coverage for tools that already ran: a prior no-change result cannot cover a candidate introduced by another correction. Candidate identity uses immutable raw-coordinate anchors; unresolved composed candidates generate explicit recheck obligations. Recheck reviewed profiles on the final label and require any independent anomaly resolution to bind its text and profile scope. Resolve original character/script suspicion from the qualified edits and final checks. Unresolved required evidence excludes the row.
-7. Apply the shared raw-text length check with identical cell/numeric exemptions again, then the unchanged content-role-specific shape, nonletter fraction, confidence and codec checks to the final label. Numeric role remains independent of `script_class=nonletter`. No inherited tall-box rule runs. CTC length is checked when the downstream contract supplies output steps; `require_ctc_steps` makes missing steps an explicit hold. This data-interface option does not select a training architecture.
+7. Apply the shared raw-text length check with identical cell/numeric exemptions again, then apply content-role-specific shape and nonletter fraction only to non-cells. For cells, alnum > 1 is the only length/shape check: no short_line, nonletter_fraction or ≥4-digit / 60% numeric_shape applies. Content issues, confidence, codec, CTC and held-out edition checks still apply to every row. Numeric role remains independent of `script_class=nonletter`. No inherited tall-box rule runs. CTC length is checked when the downstream contract supplies output steps; `require_ctc_steps` makes missing steps an explicit hold. This data-interface option does not select a training architecture.
 8. Enforce held-out edition/crop protection and exact-crop duplicate/conflicting-label rules, then export all dispositions, retained train rows, unchanged evaluation cohorts, pending corrective queues and attrition accounting.
 
 The current new entry point is `greekocr.harvest.line_pipeline_census`. Historical `admission.evaluate`, `qualified_admission` and their replay files remain available for historical consumers; they are not silently called by this pipeline. New filtered releases must use the new entry point and its exports.
 
+## Content gate: owner homoglyph ruling
+
+**Owner, 14 Oct.** Any Greek word containing a Latin, Cyrillic or other-script letter drops the whole line automatically. Examples: ΚΕΦΑΛΑΙΟN, Δαβій, Fιδον, λόγoς. There is no look-alike correction and no model pass. The earlier repair-and-admit path for such words was a deviation from the owner's rule, and gate 0.3 removes it.
+
+**Owner, 18 Oct.** The only allowance is a secondary-script WHOLE word, per class, when it has at least one letter with no look-alike in the primary script.
+
+**Implementation check (part 3, read only): absent.** `inventory()` detects mixed-script words, and `content_gate_exclusion()` drops them. `content_issues()` permits Latin under the source-level `mixed_class_or_minority` policy and flags majority Latin, or uses declared expected scripts. It has no per-class whole-word allowance conditioned on a letter without a primary-script look-alike. Part 3 records this gap without implementing it.
+
 ## Input configuration
 
 The CLI defaults to a no-processing preflight:
